  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Collections\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Collections\n       Program: commons-collections\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Collections/Collections.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-collections.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Collections/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 28\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Collections-14\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\n0725e476d4cc66e6331bdceb4e29a54a9ce7f462\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2008-11-04 03:58:37 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nCOLLECTIONS-294\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/COLLECTIONS-294\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.collections.map.TestCaseInsensitiveMap::testLocaleIndependence\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError: en: 1 expected:<value> but was:<null>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.collections.map.CaseInsensitiveMap\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: Fix case-insensitive string handling\nType: Bug | Priority: Major | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nFor example, the behavior of the {{CaseInsensitiveMap}} is currently platform-dependent, please see [Common Bug #3|http://www.nabble.com/Re%3A-Common-Bugs-p14931921s177.html] for details.\n\nComments:\n\n[Henri Yandell]: Definitely for the ExtendedProperties, it's obviously using English as a Locale.\n\nI'm less convinced by CaseInsensitiveMap. Instead it seems that either:\n\na) It should have a Locale parameter to the constructor\nb) It should be rewritten to be a CaseInsensitiveMap [ie: depend on equalsIgnoreCase], and not a ToLowerCaseMap as it currently is.\n\n[Benjamin Bentmann]: Yes, you're right, the map thing is trickier than I realized. Attached is a new patch that makes key comparisons behave as {{equalsIgnoreCase()}} would do (watch out for the extended unit test that fails when using {{String.toLowerCase()}} in {{convertKey()}}).\n\nA question that pops up is whether {{CaseInsensitiveMap}} should have been case-preserving for keys, i.e. store keys in their original case but compare case-insensitively. I mean, there seem to be two different use cases involved here:\n# case-insentive key lookup, i.e. {{map.get(\"key\") == map.get(\"KEY\")}} but possibly {{map.keySet().contains(\"Key\")}}\n# automatic key normalization to lower/upper case to provide a specific key set view\n\n[Henri Yandell]: Note: ExtendedProperties patch applied (r655204). I typo'd the key in the comment so it doesn't appear here.\n\n[Henri Yandell]: svn ci -m \"Applying Benjamin Bentmann's second patch from COLLECTIONS-294, fixing the locale issue in CaseInsensitiveMap by converting each character individually and not using toLowerCase\" src\n\nSending        src/java/org/apache/commons/collections/map/CaseInsensitiveMap.java\nSending        src/test/org/apache/commons/collections/map/TestCaseInsensitiveMap.java\nTransmitting file data ..\nCommitted revision 711168.\n\n[Sebb]: Unfortunately, Locale(String) is Java 1.4+ only, and Collections still targets 1.3.\n\nReplaced with Locale(\"tr\",\"\",\"\") - which is what Java 1.4 does anyway\n\nURL: http://svn.apache.org/viewvc?rev=744957&view=rev\nLog:\nCOLLECTIONS-294: Replace Locale(\"tr\") with Locale(\"tr\",\"\",\"\") to be Java 1.3 compliant",
  "fix_diff": ""
}